{
  "verses": [
    {
      "verse_num": 1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Keep not thou silence, O God: hold not thy peace, and be not still, O God."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ of Asaph: or, for Asaph"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "For, lo, thine enemies make a tumult: and they that hate thee have lifted up the head."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "They have taken crafty counsel against thy people, and consulted against thy hidden ones."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "They have said,"
        },
        {
          "type": "speech",
          "speaker": "The enemies of Israel",
          "text": "Come, and let us cut them off from being a nation; that the name of Israel may be no more in remembrance."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "For they have consulted together with one consent: they are confederate against thee:"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ consent: Heb. heart"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "The tabernacles of Edom, and the Ishmaelites; of Moab, and the Hagarenes;"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalek; the Philistines with the inhabitants of Tyre;"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Assur also is joined with them: they have holpen the children of Lot. Selah."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ holpen: Heb. been an arm to"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Do unto them as unto the Midianites; as to Sisera, as to Jabin, at the brook of Kison:"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Which perished at Endor: they became as dung for the earth."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Make their nobles like Oreb, and like Zeeb: yea, all their princes as Zebah, and as Zalmunna:"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 12,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Who said,"
        },
        {
          "type": "speech",
          "speaker": "Unknown",
          "text": "Let us take to ourselves the houses of God in possession."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 13,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "O my God, make them like a wheel; as the stubble before the wind."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 14,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "As the fire burneth a wood, and as the flame setteth the mountains on fire;"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 15,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "So persecute them with thy tempest, and make them afraid with thy storm."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 16,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Fill their faces with shame; that they may seek thy name, O LORD."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 17,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Let them be confounded and troubled for ever; yea, let them be put to shame, and perish:"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 18,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "That men may know that thou, whose name alone is JEHOVAH, art the most high over all the earth."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    }
  ]
}